  "reason": "Test-only repair of 32 tests/v3 files left red on origin/main because their tests were not updated when Core changed (independent validator class a). #939 (831d0d0, async storage) left synchronous callers, stubs and helpers on now-async APIs (missing awaits; plain-def stubs Core now awaits; asyncio.run inside a running loop; await inside generator expressions; a thread targeting an async def; iter_text on an async response; session.query on an AsyncSession; a missing Database.initialize(); start_chat_turn's returned producer task no longer awaited), and the budget benchmark now serves through uvicorn.Server(...).serve(), so test_core_budget_model hung on a real server; the test now patches that seam. test_approval_continuation now waits until each approval waiter has parked (bounded) instead of one sleep(0), starting the second waiter after the first as the synchronous fixture did. Memory-runner hold (64e0379, docs/design/memory-budgets.md): Host and SSH command tests use chat owners or chat-origin invocations and set NEBULA_TEMP_UNMANAGED_COMMAND_PROJECT_IDS to the test project, exactly as #976 migrated its sibling test; report renders are held unconditionally, so the reporting API test expects the hold (failed render, 409 not-ready PDF) and the renderer-level tests (note transform, glyph warnings, signed FINAL report) check the hold and render Core's saved snapshot with the importable worker entry render_pdf_snapshot. No hold is loosened. Stale expectations updated to deliberate changes: #974 (8770094) MCP context keys in goal-chat metadata; 8c49457 and #958 (0d95449) host-capacity help; #958 and 64e0379 settings destinations, host_pressure operations and memory tools; #935 (ff480db) terminal guide wording; c5120f7 required archive members. Selected: every repaired file, whole where every test passes on the branch, otherwise by node id.",
  "exclusions": "No frontend, native or Playwright cases: only Python tests under tests/v3 changed; no product, UI or API code changed, so no real-Core check applies. Left out by node id (still red, unchanged except where noted): (b, routed product bugs) test_notebooks::test_notebook_inventory_does_not_block_core_and_coalesces_scans and ::test_notebook_inventory_route_keeps_core_health_responsive (notebooks.py list_async walks the folder on the event loop since #939); test_operator_help::test_ordinary_project_conversation_gets_no_operator_help (dcf5a41 'PostgreSQL' keyword); test_packaging::test_nebula3_runtime_has_no_conditional_import_fallbacks (imports inside try bodies); test_core_budget_model::test_model_uses_current_chat_binding_after_harness_rollover (scripts/benchmarks/core_budget_model.py iterates an un-awaited find_entities). Red on origin/main 8fe806a and 3c0481c outside the validated list, not touched: test_operator_help::test_a_failure_receipt_is_searched_by_what_it_says_not_its_schema and ::test_a_failed_step_is_answered_with_its_runbook_and_not_the_mcp_article (host-capacity now also ranks for a failed-command receipt). Memory-runner hold (64e0379): test_reporting::test_pdf_is_valid_cached_and_warns_without_interpreting_content (asserts a completed render is reused from cache), ::test_pdf_export_hashes_artifacts_off_the_event_loop (asserts the cached PDF is re-verified and reused) and ::test_pdf_download_route_verifies_off_the_event_loop (asserts the download route verifies a stored PDF) need a completed Core render, which the unconditional service-level hold forbids; they are left unchanged rather than weakened. Environmental here: test_api::test_provider_chat_api_runs_selected_native_hooks hangs identically on main and branch on this saturated host (its api fixture builds create_app with the default host-load gate, so the provider turn waits for host pressure); unrelated to this change. test_product_knowledge.py is not selected: its only edited case